From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: tell when the compositor showed a window's frame

A frame Qt drew is not a frame the compositor showed. One drawn at a size
the compositor hasn't configured yet, or whose commit waits behind a
busy GUI thread, can reach the screen seconds later or never, and nothing
in Qt says when it did: Qt Wayland 6.12 binds no presentation-time.

FramePresentation, attached to any window, asks wp_presentation for
feedback on the first frame begun after ask(), from the render thread
just before that frame is drawn and committed, and answers with which
frame it was (counted as framesBegun counts) and when it was shown on
the monotonic clock, or that it was discarded. Asking again on each
answer follows every frame. With no wp_presentation global, available is
false and every ask is answered as discarded.

timesOf(frame) says when that frame's sync began and ended, its render
began and ended and it was swapped, each read on the render thread as it
happened. The GUI thread hears afterRendering and frameSwapped queued,
once it's free, so a frame timed by them includes however long the GUI
thread was busy after the sync.

---
diff --git a/src/wayland/CMakeLists.txt b/src/wayland/CMakeLists.txt
index 7bd6c15..b8881e0 100644
--- a/src/wayland/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/wayland/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -136,6 +136,9 @@ list(APPEND WAYLAND_MODULES Quickshell.Wayland._IdleNotify)
 add_subdirectory(shortcuts_inhibit)
 list(APPEND WAYLAND_MODULES Quickshell.Wayland._ShortcutsInhibitor)
 
+add_subdirectory(presentation)
+list(APPEND WAYLAND_MODULES Quickshell.Wayland._Presentation)
+
 add_subdirectory(windowmanager)
 
 # widgets for qmenu
